  "notes": "Def Jam pop-R&B across a Bloodshy-era pop crossover and the Dupri / Kwamé-orbit R&B board, 2001–2006. The research gives \"68–105 straight\" with six sourced tempos, so the mode sits at 100 and `halfTime` is false. Three drum deltas come from the two records the entry describes in detail: the 105 club cut is \"four-on-the-floor-adjacent\", hence `fourOnFloorInChorus` true and a continuous 16th hat with the open hat on both offbeats; the 85 R&B cut is \"sparse trap-adjacent 16th kick with a hard clap on 2&4\", hence a kick syncopation of 0.5 with a 0.22 tresillo lean and the secondary anchor on `2a`; and \"an Eastern-flavoured percussion layer\" is a perc/timbale/tambourine/rim bed at two to five hits a bar, which nothing else in this batch carries. Harmony is \"two-chord minor vamps with a plucked/bell riff\", so `maxChords` is 2. \"Light thin soprano in a narrow range, hook built from a short repeated cell, harmony doubled rather than stacked\" is a sixteen-semitone melody register, `twoBarCellRepeat`, a 3–5 pitch motif and a counter density of only 0.3. The low end is \"808 sub with slides on the 85–100 R&B cuts; a driving 8th-note synth bass on the club cuts\" — two behaviours, both bass parts rather than a drum-kit 808, so no `drums.bass808` block and a `glideProb` of 0.3. ⚠ Confidence is **low**: the research rates the entry medium-low and marks the key claim `[LOW-CONF]`. ⚠ Every velocity and density number is INFERRED. ⚠ `session.keys` is INFERRED: the entry's Keys line gives \"minor-mode two-chord vamps on the R&B cuts, major on the pop crossovers [LOW-CONF]\" and enumerates no tonic, so the values here and their weights are this author's reading of that line. ⚠ **`chords.harmonicRhythm` re-weighted (2026-08-17, harmony variety floor).** The entry's harmony line is \"two-chord minor vamps on the R&B cuts, major on the pop crossovers\", and the engine's `vamp` value is *one* chord held for the whole clip (`generators::chords`: \"One chord for the whole pattern\") — so weighting `vamp` at the top rendered a **one**-chord bed the research nowhere describes. The chord motion the entry states is now carried by `1_per_bar` (the pair over a 2-bar cell) and `2_bars_per_chord` (the pair over a 4-bar cell), with `vamp` kept as the minority for the held reading. ⚠ The split between those two rates is **INFERRED** — the entry names the device, not its rate.",
